# Optional. Everything has a safe default; the lab needs no tenant and no credentials of its own (its issuers and keys live in memory); only the optional Real-mode gateway check reads an agent key (FID_GW_KEY_<NAME>) from the settings file.
# The shared settings file is ~/Development/.env (mode 600; STANDALONE_ENV overrides the path), read by every standalone app.
# This lab takes one optional key from it into its environment:
# FID_LAB_MODE=mock               # the mode the page opens in: mock (default) or live (both loopback-only; only the Real-mode gateway check goes out)
# Per-run settings (shell, not the shared file; the shared file holds no PORT):
# PORT=7400                       # must be in 7400-7449
# FIDLAB_BIND=127.0.0.1           # loopback only unless you set this on purpose (the container does)
